distribution ρ = −½ ∂²M/∂Ha∂Hb on those same axes, estimated by local quadratic regression. The rotated coordinates in which FORC diagrams are conventionally drawn are overlaid as arrows. Bu runs parallel to the diagonal and Bc at right angles to it, so the diagonal Hb = Ha is simultaneously the edge of the measured region and the Bc = 0 axis.","width":"100%","align":"center","data":{"altTextIsAutoGenerated":true},"key":"xb5xJenItt","urlSource":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PmagPy/RockmagPy-notebooks/main/book/images/forc_explainer.png"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"captionNumber","kind":"figure","label":"forc_explainer","identifier":"forc_explainer","html_id":"forc-explainer","enumerator":"1","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"MQOPaeUAnj"},{"type":"text","value":"1","key":"WRK90lmfOV"},{"type":"text","value":":","key":"mSx7A8fBJ1"}],"template":"Figure %s:","key":"TmrlrmjdGg"},{"type":"text","value":"What a FORC measurement is and how the distribution follows from it, shown with the Baraboo hematite vein material example distributed with RockmagPy (measured by Maxwell Brown at the IRM). Moments are in absolute units throughout: this specimen does not reach saturation within the measured field range, so there is no meaningful M","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"key":"BxOQyqnz2G"},{"type":"subscript","children":[{"type":"text","value":"s","key":"WhZte7xHXv"}],"key":"MmAhNb2agK"},{"type":"text","value":" to normalize by. (a) One reversal curve (blue) within the major hysteresis loop (grey). The curve departs the descending branch at the reversal field H","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"key":"pAnYklCOjL"},{"type":"subscript","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a","key":"jDcjBQTyC0"}],"key":"QV9sc3fyE9"},{"type":"text","value":" (open circle) and is measu